{
  "id": "24081_assaku",
  "headword": "{圧搾|あっさく}",
  "reading": "あっさく",
  "romaji": "assaku",
  "part_of_speech": "noun, suru verb",
  "gloss": "compression; pressing; squeezing",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "compression; pressing; squeezing",
      "explanation": "The act of applying pressure to compress, squeeze out liquid, or condense something."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "24081_assaku_ex1",
      "japanese": "{圧搾|あっさく}{空気|くうき}で{機械|きかい}を{動|うご}かす。",
      "english": "The machine runs on compressed air.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "24081_assaku_ex2",
      "japanese": "オリーブを{圧搾|あっさく}して{油|あぶら}を{取|と}り{出|だ}す。",
      "english": "Extract oil by pressing olives.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "24081_assaku_ex3",
      "japanese": "この{果汁|かじゅう}は{圧搾|あっさく}{製法|せいほう}で{作|つく}られているので{風味|ふうみ}が{豊|ゆた}かだ。",
      "english": "This juice is made by the cold-press method, so it has a rich flavor.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Refers to applying mechanical pressure to squeeze, compress, or extract liquid from something. Common in industrial contexts (compressed air, hydraulic presses) and increasingly in food marketing, where {圧搾|あっさく} methods are promoted as producing higher-quality oils and juices.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {圧搾|あっさく}{空気|くうき}: compressed air\n- {圧搾|あっさく}{機|き}: pressing machine; press\n- {圧搾|あっさく}{製法|せいほう}: pressing method (for oil, juice)\n- コールド{圧搾|あっさく}: cold pressing\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {圧縮|あっしゅく}: compression — reducing volume (gas, data), not extracting liquid\n- {搾|しぼ}る: to squeeze/wring — the everyday verb for squeezing liquid out",
